Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted).
Source: https://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/v6.12.0/src/corelib/io/qprocess_unix.cpp
Source blob: 58d582b2bb2f10a5e6e2df91c9309e57fa758a84

Use a private address space for the NetBSD detached-launch intermediate child.
The child calls the forkfd fallback, which initializes process-global state.
vfork shares those state writes with the parent, but does not share sigaction.
This can leave the parent with an initialized forkfd and no SIGCHLD handler.
Keep normal QProcess launch selection and signal-mask cleanup unchanged.

--- src/corelib/io/qprocess_unix.cpp.orig
+++ src/corelib/io/qprocess_unix.cpp
@@ -358,12 +358,20 @@ struct QChildProcess
     template <typename Lambda> int doFork(Lambda &&childLambda)
     {
         pid_t pid;
+#if defined(Q_OS_NETBSD)
+        // startDetached() calls startChild() in this intermediate child.
+        // NetBSD's forkfd fallback initializes process-global state there.
+        // Keep that state private: vfork() shares the parent's address space,
+        // but changes to SIGCHLD handling belong only to the child process.
+        pid = fork();
+#else
         if (isUsingVfork) {
             QT_IGNORE_DEPRECATIONS(pid = vfork();)
         } else {
             pid = fork();
         }
+#endif
         if (pid == 0)
             _exit(childLambda());
         return pid;
     }
